      "writtenOn": "2022-11-10T03:29:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "readXmlConfig returns std::nullopt if the file can\u0027t be parsed.\n\nI copied that from PolicyConfig.h where we can potentially call read on an empty string. \nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/audio/core/all-versions/vts/functional/7.0/PolicyConfig.h;l\u003d47;drc\u003d1e703f182e2fcbb9123bf661d81d22a04d0e1f8d\n\nBut you\u0027re right; I should determine if a file is readable using the same function. I shouldn\u0027t be relying on a specific implementation of the xsdc tool\u0027s read.\n\nUsing std::nullopt, which should be functionally equivalent, but can apparently be less costly than using {}:\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/57964217/stdoptional-construct-empty-with-or-stdnullopt",
